  "worked_solution": "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in meters per second, we divide the number of meters, which is $315,$ by the number of seconds, $35.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{315}{35} & =\\frac{315\u00f75}{35\u00f75} \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{7} \\\\  & =63\u00f77 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the dolphin is $9$ meters per second. \n\nTo find the time it takes the dolphin to cover $396$ meters, we divide the distance by $9.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{time} & =\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} \\\\  & =\\frac{396}{9} \\\\  & =396\u00f79 \\\\  & =44.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes the dolphin $44$ seconds to travel $396$ meters.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
